<title>BELGIUM: LUXAIR ANNOUNCES NEW FLIGHT TO LONDON STANSTED.</title>
<headline>LUXAIR ANNOUNCES NEW FLIGHT TO LONDON STANSTED.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg airline Luxair said on Thursday it would add a new flight to London's Stansted airport, starting February 3.</p>
<p>The new service would bring Luxair's total daily connections to London airports to four, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>Luxair is 23.1 percent-owned by the Luxembourg government. Other shareholders include Germany's Lufthansa AG (13.0 percent), Banque Internationale a Luxembourg (13.1 percent) and Banque Generale du Luxembourg (12.1 percent).</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
